# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formalism for the latest version of Qiskit noise learning"
msgstr "Pormalismong matematikal para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Qiskit noise learning"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formalism"
msgstr "Mathematical formalism"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formalism {#mathematical-formalism}"
msgstr "Pormalismong matematikal {#mathematical-formalism}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Given the task of learning Pauli noise for a set of Clifford gates, a common analysis technique is to track how individual Pauli operators are transformed through a sequence of gate applications (under the assumption that the gates are Clifford and the noise is a Pauli channel, a single Pauli will always be mapped to another Pauli up to a scalar that is a function of the noise). Obviously, the evolution of *any* state under such a sequence can be captured by a linear combination of such trajectories, but under the assumption that we always prepare the state in a Pauli eigenstate, and always measure and post-process the results to compute the expectation value of a Pauli operator, the relationship between the expectation value and the noise model parameters will *always* depend on only a single such trajectory. This follows from the simple fact that the initial state is a linear combination of Pauli operators, each gate and noise model maps Paulis to Paulis and preserves their orthogonality, and the final expectation value “selects” only one of the Paulis in the final decomposition before measurement.\n"
msgstr "Kapag ang gawain ay matutunan ang Pauli noise para sa isang set ng mga Clifford gate, karaniwang technique sa pagsusuri ang pagsubaybay kung paano nagbabago ang bawat indibidwal na Pauli operator sa isang sequence ng mga paglalapat ng gate (sa ilalim ng palagay na Clifford ang mga gate at Pauli channel ang noise, ang isang Pauli ay laging mamamapa sa isa pang Pauli hanggang sa isang scalar na function ng noise). Malinaw na ang ebolusyon ng *anumang* state sa ilalim ng ganoong sequence ay maaaring makuha sa pamamagitan ng linear combination ng mga ganoong trajectory, ngunit sa ilalim ng palagay na lagi nating inihahanda ang state sa isang Pauli eigenstate, at laging sinusukat at pinoproseso ang mga resulta para kalkulahin ang expectation value ng isang Pauli operator, ang ugnayan ng expectation value at ng mga parameter ng noise model ay *laging* nakadepende sa iisang trajectory lang. Sumusunod ito sa simpleng katotohanang ang initial state ay isang linear combination ng mga Pauli operator, ang bawat gate at noise model ay nagmamapa ng mga Pauli sa mga Pauli at pinapanatili ang kanilang orthogonality, at ang huling expectation value ay “pumipili” lang ng isa sa mga Pauli sa huling decomposition bago ang measurement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This type of reasoning appears in many parallel research tracks in noise learning, including in the Pauli gate-set learning literature \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\"), [2](#id20 \"Edward H. Chen, Senrui Chen, Laurin E. Fischer, Andrew Eddins, Luke C. G. Govia, Brad Mitchell, Andre He, Youngseok Kim, Liang Jiang, and Alireza Seif. Disambiguating pauli noise in quantum computers. PRX Quantum, pages, 2026. doi:10.1103/69wc-gzl6.\")], the ACES literature \\[[3](#id15 \"Steven T. Flammia. Averaged Circuit Eigenvalue Sampling. In 17th Conference on the Theory of Quantum Computation, Communication and Cryptography (TQC 2022), volume 232 of Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs), 4:1–4:10. Dagstuhl, Germany, 2022. Schloss Dagstuhl – Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik. doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.TQC.2022.4.\")], and the cycle benchmarking literature \\[[4](#id14 \"Alexander Erhard, Joel J. Wallman, Lukas Postler, Michael Meth, Roman Stricker, Esteban A. Martinez, Philipp Schindler, Thomas Monz, Joseph Emerson, and Rainer Blatt. Characterizing large-scale quantum computers via cycle benchmarking. Nature Communications, 10(1):5347, 2019. doi:10.1038/s41467-019-13068-7.\")]. This reasoning was further generalized in \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] to include Clifford-MCM gates (a Clifford gate followed by a projective mid-circuit measurement). This package most closely follows \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\"), [5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")]. While not explicitly named, we adopt the *Pattern Transfer Graph* (PTG) formalism for describing how Pauli operators evolve through learning circuits, providing a direct data representation of *paths* through the graph.\n"
msgstr "Lumilitaw ang ganitong uri ng pangangatwiran sa maraming magkakatulad na linya ng pananaliksik sa noise learning, kabilang sa literatura ng Pauli gate-set learning \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\"), [2](#id20 \"Edward H. Chen, Senrui Chen, Laurin E. Fischer, Andrew Eddins, Luke C. G. Govia, Brad Mitchell, Andre He, Youngseok Kim, Liang Jiang, and Alireza Seif. Disambiguating pauli noise in quantum computers. PRX Quantum, pages, 2026. doi:10.1103/69wc-gzl6.\")], sa literatura ng ACES \\[[3](#id15 \"Steven T. Flammia. Averaged Circuit Eigenvalue Sampling. In 17th Conference on the Theory of Quantum Computation, Communication and Cryptography (TQC 2022), volume 232 of Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs), 4:1–4:10. Dagstuhl, Germany, 2022. Schloss Dagstuhl – Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik. doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.TQC.2022.4.\")], at sa literatura ng cycle benchmarking \\[[4](#id14 \"Alexander Erhard, Joel J. Wallman, Lukas Postler, Michael Meth, Roman Stricker, Esteban A. Martinez, Philipp Schindler, Thomas Monz, Joseph Emerson, and Rainer Blatt. Characterizing large-scale quantum computers via cycle benchmarking. Nature Communications, 10(1):5347, 2019. doi:10.1038/s41467-019-13068-7.\")]. Lalo pang pinalawak ang pangangatwirang ito sa \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] para isama ang mga Clifford-MCM gate (isang Clifford gate na sinusundan ng projective mid-circuit measurement). Ang package na ito ay pinakamalapit na sumusunod sa \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\"), [5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")]. Bagaman hindi tahasang pinangalanan, ginagamit namin ang *Pattern Transfer Graph* (PTG) formalism para ilarawan kung paano nagbabago ang mga Pauli operator sa mga learning circuit, na nagbibigay ng direktang representasyon ng data ng mga *path* sa graph.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following is a review of some core mathematical concepts from the literature. It is primarily meant to consolidate notation, and to serve as a conceptual documentation reference for the rest of the package.\n"
msgstr "Ang sumusunod ay pagbabalik-aral sa ilang pangunahing konseptong matematikal mula sa literatura. Pangunahing layunin nitong pagsama-samahin ang notasyon, at magsilbing konseptuwal na sanggunian sa dokumentasyon para sa natitirang bahagi ng package.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"background\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Background {#1-background}"
msgstr "1. Batayang kaalaman {#1-background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"notation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.1 Notation {#11-notation}"
msgstr "1.1 Notasyon {#11-notation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For $K \\in \\mathbb{N}$, let $[K] = \\{0, 1, \\dots, K - 1\\}$. For a finite set $S \\subset \\mathbb{N}$ of qubit indices, let $\\mathcal{P}^S$ denote the set of *unphased* Pauli operators acting on those qubits. Note that we think of elements of $\\mathcal{P}^S$ as functions mapping $S \\rightarrow \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}$, so that for any $P \\in \\mathcal{P}^S$ and $T \\subseteq S$, $P|_T$ denotes the restriction of $P$ to the qubit subset $T$. Along these lines, for disjoint sets $S, T$, and $P \\in \\mathcal{P}^S$ and $Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^T$, $P \\otimes Q$ denotes the element of $\\mathcal{P}^{S \\cup T}$ such that $P \\otimes Q |_S = P$ and $P \\otimes Q |_T = Q$. This notation is helpful to avoid explicitly dealing with subsystem orderings, and to make it easy to describe restrictions.\n"
msgstr "Para sa $K \\in \\mathbb{N}$, hayaang $[K] = \\{0, 1, \\dots, K - 1\\}$. Para sa isang finite set $S \\subset \\mathbb{N}$ ng mga qubit index, hayaang $\\mathcal{P}^S$ ang kumakatawan sa set ng mga *unphased* na Pauli operator na kumikilos sa mga qubit na iyon. Tandaan na iniisip natin ang mga elemento ng $\\mathcal{P}^S$ bilang mga function na nagmamapa ng $S \\rightarrow \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}$, kaya para sa anumang $P \\in \\mathcal{P}^S$ at $T \\subseteq S$, ang $P|_T$ ay tumutukoy sa restriction ng $P$ sa qubit subset na $T$. Kaugnay nito, para sa mga disjoint set na $S, T$, at $P \\in \\mathcal{P}^S$ at $Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^T$, ang $P \\otimes Q$ ay tumutukoy sa elemento ng $\\mathcal{P}^{S \\cup T}$ kung saan $P \\otimes Q |_S = P$ at $P \\otimes Q |_T = Q$. Nakakatulong ang notasyong ito para maiwasan ang tahasang pakikitungo sa mga ordering ng subsystem, at para madaling ilarawan ang mga restriction.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For finite subsets $M \\subset \\mathbb{N}$, we denote $\\mathbb{Z}_2^M$ as the set of the bit strings whose elements are indexed by $M$. Similarly to the above, we think of elements as functions mapping $M \\rightarrow \\mathbb{Z}_2$, so that we may easily describe substrings in terms of restrictions of the index set.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga finite subset na $M \\subset \\mathbb{N}$, tinutukoy natin ang $\\mathbb{Z}_2^M$ bilang set ng mga bit string na ang mga elemento ay naka-index ayon sa $M$. Gaya ng nasa itaas, iniisip natin ang mga elemento bilang mga function na nagmamapa ng $M \\rightarrow \\mathbb{Z}_2$, para madali nating mailarawan ang mga substring sa pamamagitan ng mga restriction ng index set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lastly, for a matrix $X$, we use $| X \\rangle\\!\\rangle$ to denote its vectorization. Based on the limited way in which we use this notation, it is not actually necessary to choose a specific vectorization convention. For a classical bit string $m$, we use the shorthand $| m \\rangle\\!\\rangle = | | m \\rangle\\langle m | \\rangle\\!\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Panghuli, para sa isang matrix na $X$, ginagamit natin ang $| X \\rangle\\!\\rangle$ para tukuyin ang vectorization nito. Dahil sa limitadong paraan ng paggamit natin sa notasyong ito, hindi talaga kailangang pumili ng partikular na vectorization convention. Para sa isang classical bit string na $m$, ginagamit natin ang shorthand na $| m \\rangle\\!\\rangle = | | m \\rangle\\langle m | \\rangle\\!\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"quantum-instruments\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.2 Quantum instruments {#12-quantum-instruments}"
msgstr "1.2 Mga quantum instrument {#12-quantum-instruments}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A quantum operation producing classical bits $m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$ (for example, the result of measurement) is generally modeled as a linear map of the form:\n"
msgstr "Ang isang quantum operation na gumagawa ng mga classical bit na $m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$ (halimbawa, ang resulta ng measurement) ay karaniwang imomodelo bilang isang linear map na may anyong:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
" \\rho \\mapsto \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m(\\rho) \\otimes | m \\rangle\\langle m |, \n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
" \\rho \\mapsto \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m(\\rho) \\otimes | m \\rangle\\langle m |, \n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the set $\\{\\mathcal{E}_m: m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M\\}$ are completely positive, and $\\sum_m \\mathcal{E}_m$ is trace-preserving. A set of completely positive maps $\\{\\mathcal{E}_m\\}$ satisfying these properties is called a *quantum instrument*. A unitary gate is a special case of an instrument with only one element that is a unitary operation.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang set na $\\{\\mathcal{E}_m: m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M\\}$ ay completely positive, at ang $\\sum_m \\mathcal{E}_m$ ay trace-preserving. Ang set ng mga completely positive map na $\\{\\mathcal{E}_m\\}$ na tumutupad sa mga katangiang ito ay tinatawag na *quantum instrument*. Ang unitary gate ay espesyal na kaso ng instrument na may iisang elemento lang na isang unitary operation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"noisy-clifford-mcm-reset-gates\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Noisy Clifford-MCM-reset gates {#2-noisy-clifford-mcm-reset-gates}"
msgstr "2. Mga noisy na Clifford-MCM-reset gate {#2-noisy-clifford-mcm-reset-gates}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The formalism utilized in this package assumes every gate in the gate set to be characterized consists of the following sequence of operations on $K$ qubits:\n"
msgstr "Ipinapalagay ng formalism na ginagamit sa package na ito na ang bawat gate sa gate set na kakarakterisahin ay binubuo ng sumusunod na sequence ng mga operasyon sa $K$ qubit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Clifford operation on all qubits.\n"
msgstr "Isang Clifford operation sa lahat ng qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A mid-circuit projective measurement along $Z$ on some subset of qubits $M \\subseteq [K]$.\n"
msgstr "Isang mid-circuit projective measurement sa kahabaan ng $Z$ sa ilang subset ng mga qubit na $M \\subseteq [K]$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A mid-circuit reset to the $Z$ ground state on some subset of qubits $R \\subseteq [K]$.\n"
msgstr "Isang mid-circuit reset sa $Z$ ground state sa ilang subset ng mga qubit na $R \\subseteq [K]$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is a general class of operations that includes unitary Clifford gates, measurement, state preparation, and any combination of the above. Note that we assume measurement and reset are always along the $Z$-axis for each qubit. While this is not strictly required, it is a common feature of many quantum computing modalities, and enables simplified representations and analysis.\n"
msgstr "Ito ay isang pangkalahatang klase ng mga operasyon na kinabibilangan ng mga unitary Clifford gate, measurement, state preparation, at anumang kombinasyon ng mga nabanggit. Tandaan na ipinapalagay nating ang measurement at reset ay laging nasa kahabaan ng $Z$-axis para sa bawat qubit. Bagaman hindi ito mahigpit na kinakailangan, karaniwang katangian ito ng maraming quantum computing modality, at nagbibigay-daan sa mas pinasimpleng mga representasyon at pagsusuri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As outlined in \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\"), [6](#id18 \"Stefanie J. Beale and Joel J. Wallman. Randomized compiling for subsystem measurements. 2023. URL: http://arxiv.org/abs/2304.06599, doi:10.48550/arXiv.2304.06599.\")] for the no-reset case, if a specific twirling strategy is applied to a noisy instance of such a gate, then the action of the resulting operation can be modeled mathematically as a *uniform Pauli instrument*. That is, within the quantum instrument notation, $\\mathcal{E}_m = \\mathcal{U}_mG$, where $G$ is the Clifford unitary, and:\n"
msgstr "Gaya ng inilatag sa \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\"), [6](#id18 \"Stefanie J. Beale and Joel J. Wallman. Randomized compiling for subsystem measurements. 2023. URL: http://arxiv.org/abs/2304.06599, doi:10.48550/arXiv.2304.06599.\")] para sa kasong walang reset, kung may partikular na twirling strategy na inilapat sa isang noisy na instance ng ganoong gate, ang kilos ng resultang operasyon ay maaaring imodelo sa matematika bilang isang *uniform Pauli instrument*. Ibig sabihin, sa notasyon ng quantum instrument, $\\mathcal{E}_m = \\mathcal{U}_mG$, kung saan ang $G$ ay ang Clifford unitary, at:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
" \\mathcal{U}_m = \\sum_{a,b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\Lambda_{a,b} \\otimes | m + a \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle m + b |, \n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
" \\mathcal{U}_m = \\sum_{a,b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\Lambda_{a,b} \\otimes | m + a \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle m + b |, \n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where each $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ is a sub-normalized Pauli channel on the unmeasured qubits $N = [K] \\setminus M$. It is implied by this being a quantum instrument that $\\sum_{a,b} \\Lambda_{a,b}$ is also trace-preserving. Some notes:\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang bawat $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ ay isang sub-normalized na Pauli channel sa mga hindi sinukat na qubit na $N = [K] \\setminus M$. Ipinahihiwatig ng pagiging quantum instrument nito na ang $\\sum_{a,b} \\Lambda_{a,b}$ ay trace-preserving din. Ilang tala:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The initial untwirled noise is modeled to include both “quantum” and “classical” errors: erroneous operations on the quantum registers, as well as mistakes in the measurement value reporting.\n"
msgstr "Ang paunang untwirled na noise ay imomodelo na kinabibilangan ng parehong “quantum” at “classical” na error: mga maling operasyon sa mga quantum register, pati na mga pagkakamali sa pag-ulat ng halaga ng measurement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The noise map $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ is *independent* of the measurement outcome $m$.\n"
msgstr "Ang noise map na $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ ay *independent* sa measurement outcome na $m$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In words, a single term in the above sum represents observing a measurement outcome of $m$ when the measured state was $| m + b \\rangle$ (a misclassification if $b \\neq 0$), and when the output state on the measurement register is $| m + a \\rangle$ (the “wrong” state when $a \\neq 0$). The map $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ simultaneously encodes the action on the unmeasured qubits (conditioned on the measurement behavior) and the *probability* of the specific measurement behavior (through the normalization).\n"
msgstr "Sa madaling salita, ang isang termino sa nabanggit na sum ay kumakatawan sa pagmamasid ng measurement outcome na $m$ noong ang sinukat na state ay $| m + b \\rangle$ (isang misclassification kung $b \\neq 0$), at noong ang output state sa measurement register ay $| m + a \\rangle$ (ang “maling” state kapag $a \\neq 0$). Sabay na ine-encode ng map na $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ ang kilos sa mga hindi sinukat na qubit (na nakasalalay sa kilos ng measurement) at ang *probability* ng partikular na kilos ng measurement (sa pamamagitan ng normalization).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that we are not concerned here with the specifics of the twirling strategy: that such a strategy exists to put the channel into the above form is enough. Note that “finer” twirling strategies exist which can further restrict the form of the Pauli channels \\[[7](#id19 \"Ewout van den Berg and Pawel Wocjan. Techniques for learning sparse Pauli-Lindblad noise models. Quantum, 8:1556, 2024. URL: https://quantum-journal.org/papers/q-2024-12-10-1556/, doi:10.22331/q-2024-12-10-1556.\")]; however, we take the above form as the most general mathematical representation under consideration.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na hindi natin dito inaalala ang mga detalye ng twirling strategy: sapat na na may ganoong strategy para ilagay ang channel sa nabanggit na anyo. Tandaan din na may mga “mas pinong” twirling strategy na maaaring higit pang magtakda ng limitasyon sa anyo ng mga Pauli channel \\[[7](#id19 \"Ewout van den Berg and Pawel Wocjan. Techniques for learning sparse Pauli-Lindblad noise models. Quantum, 8:1556, 2024. URL: https://quantum-journal.org/papers/q-2024-12-10-1556/, doi:10.22331/q-2024-12-10-1556.\")]; gayunpaman, kinukuha natin ang nabanggit na anyo bilang pinakapangkalahatang matematikal na representasyon na isinasaalang-alang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In Lemma 1 of \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")], it is shown that $\\mathcal{E}_m = \\mathcal{U}_mG$ can be rewritten as:\n"
msgstr "Sa Lemma 1 ng \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")], ipinapakita na ang $\\mathcal{E}_m = \\mathcal{U}_mG$ ay maaaring isulat muli bilang:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"equation-clifford-mcm-form\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
" \\mathcal{E}_m = \\frac{1}{2^{2|M| + |N|}}\\sum_{x, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^N} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y)}\n"
"\\lambda^Q_{x, y}| Q \\otimes Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes Z^x) |. \n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
" \\mathcal{E}_m = \\frac{1}{2^{2|M| + |N|}}\\sum_{x, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^N} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y)}\n"
"\\lambda^Q_{x, y}| Q \\otimes Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes Z^x) |. \n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for some real numbers $\\lambda_{x,y}^Q$, which are called the *fidelities* of the instrument.\n"
msgstr "para sa ilang real number na $\\lambda_{x,y}^Q$, na tinatawag na mga *fidelity* ng instrument.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding reset to this picture is relatively straightforward. A noisy reset operation on qubits $R \\subset [K]$ can be modeled according to the decomposition:\n"
msgstr "Medyo diretso ang pagdaragdag ng reset sa larawang ito. Ang isang noisy na reset operation sa mga qubit na $R \\subset [K]$ ay maaaring imodelo ayon sa decomposition:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"equation-reset-form\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
" \\frac{1}{2^{|R|}}\\sum_{r \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{R}} \\lambda_r | Z^r \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle I_R |. \n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
" \\frac{1}{2^{|R|}}\\sum_{r \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{R}} \\lambda_r | Z^r \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle I_R |. \n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The above form explicitly utilizes the assumption that the reset is along the $Z$-axis for each qubit. Noise in the operation is encoded in the reset fidelities $\\lambda_r$, which are simply indexed by qubit subsets.\n"
msgstr "Tahasang ginagamit ng nabanggit na anyo ang palagay na ang reset ay nasa kahabaan ng $Z$-axis para sa bawat qubit. Ang noise sa operasyon ay naka-encode sa mga reset fidelity na $\\lambda_r$, na ini-index lang ayon sa mga qubit subset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An analog to Equation [(1)](#equation-clifford-mcm-form) that includes a reset operation at the end can be attained by simply composing it with Equation [(2)](#equation-reset-form). This composition, after some simplification, yields:\n"
msgstr "Ang katumbas ng Equation [(1)](#equation-clifford-mcm-form) na may reset operation sa dulo ay makukuha sa simpleng pag-compose nito sa Equation [(2)](#equation-reset-form). Ang composition na ito, pagkatapos ng ilang pagpapasimple, ay nagbibigay ng:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split} \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}} \\sum_{\\substack{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ Q \\in\n"
"\\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y|_M)} \\lambda^Q_{x,y}  | Q \\otimes\n"
"Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |. \\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split} \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}} \\sum_{\\substack{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ Q \\in\n"
"\\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y|_M)} \\lambda^Q_{x,y}  | Q \\otimes\n"
"Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |. \\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This decomposition indicates that the number of fidelities $\\lambda^Q_{x, y}$ is\n"
msgstr "Ipinapahiwatig ng decomposition na ito na ang bilang ng mga fidelity na $\\lambda^Q_{x, y}$ ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"equation-num-fidelities\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"4^{|N \\setminus R|} 2^{|M|}2^{|M \\cup R|} = 4^{K}2^{|M|}2^{-|M \\cup R|} = 4^K 2^{-|R \\setminus M|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"4^{|N \\setminus R|} 2^{|M|}2^{|M \\cup R|} = 4^{K}2^{|M|}2^{-|M \\cup R|} = 4^K 2^{-|R \\setminus M|}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider limiting cases: (1) For no measurement or reset, $M = R = \\emptyset$, and the expression yields $4^K$, the number of phase-less Pauli operators on $K$ qubits. (2) For $M = \\emptyset$ and $R=[K]$, this yields $2^K$, which is the number of subsets of $[K]$. Lastly, (3) for $M = [K]$ and $R = \\emptyset$, this yields $4^K$. Note that this may initially seem surprising: for standard learning, measurement and reset are typically considered to have the same number of fidelities: $2^K$. However, here the all-measurement gate in this context is understood not as a *terminal* measurement, but as an MCM, and as such fidelities corresponding to non-identity *outputs* of the measurement are also included (such as $y \\neq 0$ in Equation [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form)).\n"
msgstr "Isaalang-alang ang mga limiting case: (1) Kung walang measurement o reset, $M = R = \\emptyset$, at ang expression ay nagbibigay ng $4^K$, ang bilang ng mga phase-less na Pauli operator sa $K$ qubit. (2) Para sa $M = \\emptyset$ at $R=[K]$, nagbibigay ito ng $2^K$, na siyang bilang ng mga subset ng $[K]$. Panghuli, (3) para sa $M = [K]$ at $R = \\emptyset$, nagbibigay ito ng $4^K$. Tandaan na maaaring nakakagulat ito sa una: sa karaniwang learning, ang measurement at reset ay karaniwang itinuturing na may parehong bilang ng mga fidelity: $2^K$. Gayunpaman, dito, ang all-measurement gate sa kontekstong ito ay hindi ituturing na *terminal* na measurement, kundi isang MCM, at dahil dito, kasama rin ang mga fidelity na tumutugma sa mga non-identity na *output* ng measurement (gaya ng $y \\neq 0$ sa Equation [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, it is important to note that any twirling strategy yielding the form in Equation [(1)](#equation-clifford-mcm-form) in the non-reset case still applies equally well to the non-trivial reset case with a simple modification. The potential problem is that such a twirling strategy may require operations on measured qubits *after* the measurement. Therefore, if a qubit is measured *and* reset, implementing the strategy seemingly requires inserting operations *within* the gate between the measurement and reset. However, given the nature of reset, any such operations have no effect, and can simply be skipped while still yielding the same desired structure.\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, mahalagang tandaan na ang anumang twirling strategy na nagbibigay ng anyo sa Equation [(1)](#equation-clifford-mcm-form) sa kasong walang reset ay maaari ding ilapat nang pantay na mahusay sa kasong may non-trivial na reset, sa tulong ng simpleng pagbabago. Ang posibleng problema ay maaaring mangailangan ang ganoong twirling strategy ng mga operasyon sa mga sinukat na qubit *pagkatapos* ng measurement. Samakatuwid, kung ang isang qubit ay sinukat *at* ni-reset, tila kailangan ng implementasyon ng strategy na maglagay ng mga operasyon *sa loob* ng gate sa pagitan ng measurement at reset. Gayunpaman, dahil sa likas ng reset, walang epekto ang anumang ganoong operasyon, at maaari na lang itong lagpasan habang nakukuha pa rin ang parehong ninanais na istruktura.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"path-formalism\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Path formalism {#3-path-formalism}"
msgstr "3. Pormalismo ng path {#3-path-formalism}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As described in the introduction, all learning algorithms for Pauli-type noise on Clifford gates are based around tracking how individual Paulis evolve through a circuit, picking up noise fidelity factors along the way. The expectation values of a circuit composed of such gates are therefore related simply to products of the underlying fidelities of the individual gates, and in this way model parameters can be inferred by *inverting* whatever sparse parameter-to-fidelity mapping is being assumed.\n"
msgstr "Gaya ng inilarawan sa panimula, ang lahat ng learning algorithm para sa Pauli-type na noise sa mga Clifford gate ay nakabatay sa pagsubaybay kung paano nagbabago ang mga indibidwal na Pauli sa isang circuit, habang nakakakuha ng mga noise fidelity factor sa daan. Kaya ang mga expectation value ng isang circuit na binubuo ng ganoong mga gate ay simpleng nauugnay sa mga produkto ng pinagbabatayang mga fidelity ng mga indibidwal na gate, at sa ganitong paraan ay mahuhulaan ang mga parameter ng modelo sa pamamagitan ng *pag-invert* ng anumang sparse na parameter-to-fidelity mapping na ipinapalagay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\")], in the context of unitary gate sets, this is formalized into the *Pattern Transfer Graph* (PTG): a directed graph describing all possible experiments consisting of elements of the gate set and layers of single-qubit Clifford gates (assumed to be perfect, or “free”, operations). This was generalized in \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] to include gate sets with mid-circuit measurements. In both cases, each experiment is described by tracking a single Pauli operator through the circuit, under the assumption of a particular observable being computed at each measurement site. Here we do not directly review the graph or path constructions; however, we present the required facts for justifying them within our own notation and with resets included.\n"
msgstr "Sa \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\")], sa konteksto ng mga unitary gate set, pormal itong inilalatag bilang *Pattern Transfer Graph* (PTG): isang directed graph na naglalarawan sa lahat ng posibleng eksperimentong binubuo ng mga elemento ng gate set at mga layer ng single-qubit Clifford gate (na ipinapalagay na perpekto, o “libre”, na mga operasyon). Pinalawak ito sa \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] para isama ang mga gate set na may mid-circuit measurement. Sa parehong kaso, ang bawat eksperimento ay inilalarawan sa pamamagitan ng pagsubaybay sa iisang Pauli operator sa circuit, sa ilalim ng palagay na may partikular na observable na kinakalkula sa bawat measurement site. Dito, hindi natin direktang rerepasuhin ang mga konstruksyon ng graph o path; gayunpaman, inilalahad natin ang mga kinakailangang katotohanan para bigyang-katwiran ang mga ito sa sarili nating notasyon at kasama ang mga reset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While the tracking of a single Pauli operator through the circuit may be intuitive in the unitary gate set case, it does not so obviously hold in the more general Clifford-MCM-reset case, due to the non-deterministic nature of measurement. The following proposition recovers this picture even in the more general case \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")]:\n"
msgstr "Bagaman maaaring intuitive ang pagsubaybay sa iisang Pauli operator sa circuit sa kaso ng unitary gate set, hindi ito gaanong halata sa mas pangkalahatang kaso ng Clifford-MCM-reset, dahil sa non-deterministic na likas ng measurement. Binabawi ng sumusunod na proposisyon ang larawang ito kahit sa mas pangkalahatang kaso \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")]:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Proposition 1\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  <span id=\"proof-content\" />\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Proposisyon 1\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  <span id=\"proof-content\" />\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  For any $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$, $y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R}$, and $Q\\in \\mathcal{P}^{N \\setminus R}$, it holds that:\n"
msgstr "  Para sa anumang $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$, $y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R}$, at $Q\\in \\mathcal{P}^{N \\setminus R}$, totoo na:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\n"
msgstr "$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y |\\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} |_M \\left(\\sum_{m\\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\right)\n"
"= \\lambda_{x,y}^Q\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y |\\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} |_M \\left(\\sum_{m\\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\right)\n"
"= \\lambda_{x,y}^Q\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In other words, if we compute the expectation value $Z^{x + y|_M}$ on the classical register output by the MCM, then the “Heisenberg picture” evolution of an observable through the Clifford-MCM-reset gate maps $Q \\otimes Z^y \\rightarrow Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x$. This fact alone enables recovery of PTG-like analysis beyond the unitary gate set case: with a particular post-processing of the measurement results, even gates with measurements and resets can be viewed as deterministically mapping one Pauli operator to another.\n"
msgstr "Sa madaling salita, kung kakalkulahin natin ang expectation value na $Z^{x + y|_M}$ sa classical register na inilalabas ng MCM, ang “Heisenberg picture” na ebolusyon ng isang observable sa Clifford-MCM-reset gate ay nagmamapa ng $Q \\otimes Z^y \\rightarrow Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x$. Ang katotohanang ito lang ay nagbibigay-daan sa pagbawi ng PTG-like na pagsusuri lampas sa kaso ng unitary gate set: sa isang partikular na post-processing ng mga resulta ng measurement, kahit ang mga gate na may measurement at reset ay maaaring ituring na deterministikong nagmamapa ng isang Pauli operator sa isa pa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before proving this, we write Equation [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form) in a more suggestive way. Note that for $x, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$, it holds that $Z^{x+y} = \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y)}| m \\rangle\\langle m |$, and as such (in super operator notation) we have:\n"
msgstr "Bago patunayan ito, isusulat natin ang Equation [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form) sa mas nagpapahiwatig na paraan. Tandaan na para sa $x, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$, totoo na $Z^{x+y} = \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y)}| m \\rangle\\langle m |$, at dahil dito (sa super operator notation) mayroon tayong:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split} \\begin{aligned} \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle_M = \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}}\\sum_{\\substack{x \\in\n"
"\\mathbb{Z}_2^M, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} \\lambda^Q_{x,y}  | Q \\otimes Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\n"
"\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) | \\otimes | Z^{x + y|_M} \\rangle\\!\\rangle_M, \\end{aligned} \\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split} \\begin{aligned} \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle_M = \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}}\\sum_{\\substack{x \\in\n"
"\\mathbb{Z}_2^M, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} \\lambda^Q_{x,y}  | Q \\otimes Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\n"
"\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) | \\otimes | Z^{x + y|_M} \\rangle\\!\\rangle_M, \\end{aligned} \\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where we have applied Equation [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form) and collected terms, and we use the subscript $M$ to indicate the classical measurement result register, which we treat above in a similar notation to the quantum registers.\n"
msgstr "kung saan inilapat natin ang Equation [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form) at pinagsama ang mga termino, at ginagamit natin ang subscript na $M$ para ipahiwatig ang classical measurement result register, na tinatrato natin sa itaas sa katulad na notasyon ng mga quantum register.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Proof. It holds that:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Patunay. Totoo na:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y | \\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} | \\left(\\sum_{m\\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\right)\\\\\n"
"&= \\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y | \\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} | \\left( \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}} \\sum_{\\substack{a \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ P \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} \\lambda^P_{a,b}  | P \\otimes Z^b \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(P \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^a) | \\otimes | Z^{a + b|_M} \\rangle\\!\\rangle \\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{1}{2^{2|M| + |N|}}\\sum_{\\substack{a \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ P \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N \\setminus R}}} \\lambda^P_{a, b}\\underbrace{\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y, P \\otimes Z^b \\rangle}_{2^{|M| + |N|} \\delta_{P, Q}\\delta_{y,b}} \\underbrace{\\langle Z^{x + y|_M}, Z^{a + b|_M} \\rangle}_{2^{|M|}\\delta_{x+y|_M,a+b|_M}}\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(P \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^a) |\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y | \\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} | \\left(\\sum_{m\\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\right)\\\\\n"
"&= \\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y | \\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} | \\left( \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}} \\sum_{\\substack{a \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ P \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} \\lambda^P_{a,b}  | P \\otimes Z^b \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(P \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^a) | \\otimes | Z^{a + b|_M} \\rangle\\!\\rangle \\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{1}{2^{2|M| + |N|}}\\sum_{\\substack{a \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ P \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N \\setminus R}}} \\lambda^P_{a, b}\\underbrace{\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y, P \\otimes Z^b \\rangle}_{2^{|M| + |N|} \\delta_{P, Q}\\delta_{y,b}} \\underbrace{\\langle Z^{x + y|_M}, Z^{a + b|_M} \\rangle}_{2^{|M|}\\delta_{x+y|_M,a+b|_M}}\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(P \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^a) |\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Lastly, observe that $\\delta_{y,b}\\delta_{x+y|_M,a+b|_M} = \\delta_{y,b}\\delta_{x,a}$, and hence the final term above collapses down to the single term $\\lambda^Q_{x,y} \\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |$, yielding the desired result.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Panghuli, pansinin na $\\delta_{y,b}\\delta_{x+y|_M,a+b|_M} = \\delta_{y,b}\\delta_{x,a}$, kaya ang huling termino sa itaas ay bumabagsak sa iisang terminong $\\lambda^Q_{x,y} \\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |$, na nagbibigay ng ninanais na resulta.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "See \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] for development beyond this point: the definition of the PTG, paths through the PTG, and the proof that any properly-defined path corresponds to an experiment.\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] para sa pagpapatuloy mula rito: ang depinisyon ng PTG, mga path sa PTG, at ang patunay na ang anumang wastong nadefine na path ay tumutugma sa isang eksperimento.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "References {#references}"
msgstr "Mga Sanggunian {#references}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"id17\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[1]\n"
msgstr "\\[1]\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
